// Where an agent that runs on the owner's accounts runs (0.2 list, line 22), and where each LLM call coordd runs itself
// goes: the router's choice of the place that serves a model (accounts/router.rs; the owner, N-1104 p676: "one
// component that sits in front of the gateway ... call it a router"). The model is decisions.eflint's; this file
// says only where it runs. His rule, 20 Nov 08:55: "try to load balance new placements of agents round robin across
// one tier, move to the next tier if no space". coordd asks `account-for` at each start of such an agent, a first
// start, a restart and a move alike (accounts/router.rs `take`, under the accounts' lock, where it also binds the
// answer), and for each call (`Router::call`, binding nothing), with the model asked (`call.model`), and supplies the
// facts below for that moment. An agent already on an account that can take requests keeps it (a restart is not a
// move); the rule places the others. A project says otherwise in a file of its own named placement.eflint, which
// replaces this one.

// The places: each of his accounts by its id, and "the gateway" where the coord has the gateway.
Fact place Identified by String
// The tier he put each in (the Accounts page's Priority), the highest first. The gateway's is written here until the
// window sets it: 0, under every tier the window gives an account (1 and up), so it is the last, where agents go when
// no account has space.
Fact place-tier Identified by place * Int
+place-tier("the gateway", 0).
// It can take requests now: signed in, not out, not refused, not deaf, not being removed (coordd).
Fact usable Identified by place
// Its plan as Claude Code names it (`claude auth status`'s subscriptionType: pro, max, team, enterprise), and its
// weekly use in whole per cent (rounded down) as last seen, while that week lasts (coordd, from what Claude Code said;
// none known, none supplied).
Fact plan Identified by place * String
Fact weekly-used Identified by place * Int
// Its place in its tier's round: 0 is the next after the one chosen last in that tier (coordd, from turn.json).
Fact turn Identified by place * Int
// Messages are not known to reach its sessions: none has entered a session's input on it since its sign-in, or
// since one handed to a session on it was never seen there (coordd, state.json `heard`); and how many agents of his,
// of any coord, run on it (its bindings).
Fact unheard Identified by place
Fact taken Identified by place * Int
// It serves the model asked, by the gateway's id (claude-sonnet-5-5; `call.model`, its `:EFFORT` left off): an account
// of Claude Code each of Anthropic's own (claude-...), a variant as claude-fable-5-2[1m] too; an opencode account its
// provider's (only those of the agent's provider are asked); the gateway those its lists name, by base id, and one
// they stopped naming until ten minutes of them lacked it, and every model before one was read (coordd).
Fact serves Identified by place * String
// The `--model` Claude Code is given when a call runs on his accounts, by the gateway's id (a call of a model with no
// row here runs elsewhere). They are the gateway's own Claude models (CLIProxyAPI's
// internal/registry/models/models.json, its `claude` part), so a call or an agent that goes from the gateway to an
// account finds the same models under the same names, and the models the policy chooses among do not change (coordd
// adds these to the gateway's list while one of his Claude Code accounts is signed in).
Fact claude-code-model Identified by String * String
+claude-code-model("claude-opus-5-5", "claude-opus-5-5").
+claude-code-model("claude-sonnet-5-5", "claude-sonnet-5-5").
+claude-code-model("claude-haiku-5-5", "claude-haiku-5-5").
+claude-code-model("claude-fable-5-2", "claude-fable-5-2").
+claude-code-model("claude-fable-5-1", "claude-fable-5-1").
+claude-code-model("claude-fable-5", "claude-fable-5").
+claude-code-model("claude-opus-5", "claude-opus-5").
+claude-code-model("claude-sonnet-5", "claude-sonnet-5").
+claude-code-model("claude-opus-4-8", "claude-opus-4-8").
+claude-code-model("claude-opus-4-7", "claude-opus-4-7").
+claude-code-model("claude-opus-4-6", "claude-opus-4-6").
+claude-code-model("claude-sonnet-4-6", "claude-sonnet-4-6").
+claude-code-model("claude-opus-4-5-20251101", "claude-opus-4-5-20251101").
+claude-code-model("claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929", "claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929").
+claude-code-model("claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001").
+claude-code-model("claude-opus-4-1-20250805", "claude-opus-4-1-20250805").
+claude-code-model("claude-opus-4-20250514", "claude-opus-4-20250514").
+claude-code-model("claude-sonnet-4-20250514", "claude-sonnet-4-20250514").
+claude-code-model("claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219", "claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219").
+claude-code-model("claude-3-5-haiku-20241022", "claude-3-5-haiku-20241022").

// The weekly use at or over which an account of a plan has no space for a new agent, and its 5-hour window is not
// opened: the gateway's window opener's ceilings (its service_window_opener.go names the plans claude_pro and
// claude_max), one place for both (paper-research N-412 post 2089). A plan not named here has no ceiling. The 5-hour
// window is no space line: an account at its 5-hour limit is out, and below it the window starts again within hours.
Fact weekly-ceiling Identified by String * Int
+weekly-ceiling("pro", 70).
+weekly-ceiling("max", 80).

Decision account-for
  Options place
  Requires usable(option)
  Requires serves(option, call.model)
// no space at its plan's weekly ceiling: such an account is passed over for any place that has space, in its tier or
// the next. Where none has (no gateway, and every account that can take one at its ceiling), the agent runs on one of
// them all the same, by tier and turn: it does not stand still (the owner, 20 Nov 08:45: "blocking everybody because
// one account goes down is not okay").
Prefer for account-for When weekly-used(option) >= weekly-ceiling(plan(option)):
  minimise 1
// messages not yet known to reach it, with agents on it already: such an account takes one agent, whose messages say
// whether more may come, and the next go where that is known, or through the gateway (on 20 Nov a Team seat with
// channels off took 35 agents, none of which heard a message). Where nothing else can take them, they go there all the
// same. Found deaf, it takes none and its agents move (coordd: `usable`).
Prefer for account-for When unheard(option):
  minimise taken(option)
// The first tier that has space, the highest first.
Prefer for account-for:
  maximise place-tier(option)
// Round robin within it.
Prefer for account-for:
  minimise turn(option)
